; mirroring an expression tree preserves its INTERNAL-node count: nodes(mirror e) = nodes e.
; Derived with NO induction, purely from prior theorems: count(mirror e) = count e [count-mirror, itself composed], and count x = s(nodes x) [the leaf/internal identity] applied at both mirror e and e, give s(nodes(mirror e)) = count(mirror e) = count e = s(nodes e); successor-injectivity then strips the s. A SECOND-ORDER composition -- built on count-mirror which was already a composition -- showing the Expr-AST theory now layers derived results on derived results.
